@fchollet 

Thanks for the clarification. This is really encouraging for me. I will try to get the best accuracy as I can. 

Myself and @sayakpaul were discussing about converting PyTorch weights to TF weights in case the training doesn't turn out well (as a last resort). What do you think about that?

@fchollet 

Are you saying we should go for weight conversion rather than training? 

Some people have reported lesser accuracies (timm and one other implementation) for RegNets. Personally I think training models is better than just porting over the weights. We can quantify the discrepancy if any. Also the point of RegNets as far as I understand is that they are efficient and scalable. What do you think?

@fchollet 

Understood. Thanks for the clarification. 

I've made the requested changes. Please review again. If there aren't any changes I'll start training soon.

